<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      The ONE capability the app claims (banshee-jie, ruled 2026-10-12): a banner
      posted at UNNotificationInterruptionLevel.timeSensitive is presented
      immediately and through Focus only when the running code carries this
      entitlement; without it macOS silently presents the banner as .active
      (auto-dismissed, withheld under Focus). Shrieking and a red disk ask for it
      (swift/Sources/BansheeCore/Notifications.swift).

      This is a RESTRICTED entitlement (com.apple.developer.*, TN3125): the signed
      app must also embed a Developer ID provisioning profile that authorises it,
      or amfid kills the app at launch. An ad-hoc build cannot carry it at all
      (probed 2026-10-15: SIGKILL, exit 137), so scripts/build-app.sh applies this
      file ONLY on the Developer ID path, together with the profile, and adds the
      application-identifier / team-identifier entitlements there — they are
      derived from the signing identity, not written here.

      No critical-alerts key: ruled out 2026-09-22 (Notifications.swift).
    -->
    <key>com.apple.developer.usernotifications.time-sensitive</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
